ref 1079 #uuid "68aed225-1b65-5210-aa67-e6df22bc4d41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272030 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272030 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140132" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272030 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272030 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${C}^{36},$ where\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[18]{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[36]{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272030 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a83d9fbf-2f37-5a9f-b9ba-27fe8d23afc4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272030 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have been given the following diagonalization of $C:$\n\n$$\nC={{[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{P}{{[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[18]{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[36]{3}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{D}{{{[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nSince $C=PD{P}^{-1}$, we can compute ${C}^{k}$ by using the formula \n\n$$\n{C}^{k}=P{D}^{k}{P}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nCarrying out the necessary multiplication, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{36} & =P{D}^{36}{P}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[18]{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt[36]{3}\\end{aligned}]}^{36}(\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}(\\sqrt[18]{3})^{36} & 0 \\\\ 0 & (\\sqrt[36]{3})^{36}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{3}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {3}^{1}\\